# Flags belong to a user and a message, not to a mailbox, so one
# message in two mailboxes has one set of flags: a keyword set in one
# of them shows up in the other, and so does \Seen.
#
# The watcher examines rather than selects, so that it does not take
# the \Recent claim away from main.
depends empty-inbox
send 1
a create flagscope
receive 1
a OK done
send 8
b append inbox () {168+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
Subject: one message, two mailboxes
Date: Thu, 20 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

body

receive 4
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
b OK [APPENDUID 1 1] done
send 1
c copy 1 flagscope
receive 1
c OK [COPYUID 1 1 1] done
send 1
d store 1 +flags (kiwi)
receive 4
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen kiwi)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen kiwi \*)] permanent flags
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent kiwi))
d OK done
protocol imap watcher
receive 1
* OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 AUTH=ANONYMOUS AUTH=CRAM-MD5 AUTH=DIGEST-MD5 AUTH=PLAIN AUTH=LOGIN COMPRESS=DEFLATE ENABLE ID SASL-IR STARTTLS] imapscript.test.oryx.com Archiveopteryx IMAP Server (security checking disabled)
send 2
w1 login script script
w2 examine flagscope
receive 9
w1 OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 ACL APPENDLIMIT=38400000 BINARY CHILDREN COMPRESS=DEFLATE CONDSTORE ENABLE ESEARCH I18NLEVEL=1 ID IDLE LIST-EXTENDED LITERAL+ MOVE MULTIAPPEND NAMESPACE OBJECTID QUOTA QRESYNC RIGHTS=ekntx SORT SORT=DISPLAY SPECIAL-USE STARTTLS THREAD=ORDEREDSUBJECT THREAD=REFS THREAD=REFERENCES UIDONLY UIDPLUS UNSELECT UTF8=ACCEPT WITHIN] done
* 1 EXISTS
* 1 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen kiwi)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen kiwi \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
w2 OK [READ-ONLY] done
# the copy has the keyword that was set on the original
send 1
w3 fetch 1 flags
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (FLAGS (\Recent kiwi))
w3 OK done
use main
send 1
e store 1 +flags \seen
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent \Seen kiwi))
e OK done
# ... and \Seen set in one mailbox is set in the other
use watcher
send 1
w4 fetch 1 flags
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (FLAGS (\Recent \Seen kiwi))
w4 OK done
use main
send 1
f store 1 -flags (kiwi)
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (UID 1 FLAGS (\Recent \Seen))
f OK done
# removing it in one removes it in the other
use watcher
send 1
w5 fetch 1 flags
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (FLAGS (\Recent \Seen))
w5 OK done
end
